Subject: [PATCH] MediaProfiles: do not register the VideoEditorProfile natives

Carried over from the Huawei Y210 work, where FindClass failed for it
and the non-zero return aborted zygote. Check Movie Studio on vee4ss.

---
diff --git a/media/jni/android_media_MediaProfiles.cpp b/media/jni/android_media_MediaProfiles.cpp
index 3fbb8ba09ba..832162c8dd9 100644
--- a/media/jni/android_media_MediaProfiles.cpp
+++ b/media/jni/android_media_MediaProfiles.cpp
@@ -434,11 +434,13 @@ int register_android_media_MediaProfiles(JNIEnv *env)
                gMethodsForCameraProfileClass,
                NELEM(gMethodsForCameraProfileClass));
 
-    int ret5 = AndroidRuntime::registerNativeMethods(env,
-               kVideoEditorProfileClassPathName,
-               gMethodsForVideoEditorProfileClass,
-               NELEM(gMethodsForVideoEditorProfileClass));
+    // VideoEditorProfile's native registration is skipped: FindClass fails
+    // for it on this build (VideoEditor isn't shipped as a product package
+    // here), and AndroidRuntime::startReg() aborts zygote on any non-zero
+    // return from this function, so a failing ret5 here is fatal to boot.
+    (void)kVideoEditorProfileClassPathName;
+    (void)gMethodsForVideoEditorProfileClass;
 
     // Success if all return values from above are 0
-    return (ret1 || ret2 || ret3 || ret4 || ret5);
+    return (ret1 || ret2 || ret3 || ret4);
 }
